Third-party components
======================

lwIP TCP/IP stack
-----------------
Location: Tunnel/lwip/

This project vendors a copy of the lwIP lightweight TCP/IP stack, originally
written by Adam Dunkels and maintained by lwIP contributors. lwIP is
distributed under a BSD 3-Clause style license. The full text is reproduced in
Tunnel/lwip/COPYING, which matches the per-file headers carried by the vendored
sources. Principal copyright holder:

    Copyright (c) 2001-2004 Swedish Institute of Computer Science.
    All rights reserved.

Individual files in the vendored tree carry additional copyright lines from
their own authors (Axon Digital Design B.V., Inico Technologies Ltd., Leon
Woestenberg, Simon Goldschmidt, Dominik Spies, Jasper Verschueren, Verisure
Innovation AB, Elias Oenal, Dirk Ziegelmeier, Erik Andersson, Benjamin Aigner,
Joel Cunningham / Garmin International, Deltatee Enterprises, CITEL
Technologies, Marc Boucher / MBSI, and others). Those per-file headers are the
authoritative record and must be preserved.

A scan of all 296 .c/.h files under Tunnel/lwip found no GPL or LGPL licensed
code. The lwIP license is permissive and compatible with the MIT terms above,
so combining lwIP with WSBridge source imposes no copyleft obligations. Note
that the PPP support files under Tunnel/lwip/netif/ppp (including its polarssl
subdirectory, which is BSD licensed, not GPL) are present in the tree but are
not compiled: PPP_SUPPORT is not defined in Tunnel/lwipopts.h.

If you redistribute WSBridge in binary form, reproduce the lwIP copyright
notices and license terms for the vendored files you ship, and keep
Tunnel/lwip/COPYING alongside this file.
